const e="gibraltar-international-drama-festival",h=2026,t="Whole 8-page 2026 Rules PDF read, plus the organiser's two 2026 press releases. The Rules print no street address for Ince's Hall Theatre, no phone or email (taken from the press releases), no entry form link (taken from the entry call press release) and no split of the 100 Best Play points across the five criteria. The Rules print the Festival as Monday 23 to Saturday 28 March 2026; the later press release gives Monday 23 to Friday 27 March (Gala Night on the Friday), which is used here. The press release says each participating group receives a small grant and that non-competitive entries are accepted; the Rules print only the expense claim of up to GBP 200 per entry and the restricted non-competing basis for plays that may cause offence. Adjudicator named in the press release as a member of the Guild of Drama Adjudicators (UK): not in the Rules. Dates are for the 2026 edition and are the starting suggestion for the next one.",a=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Gibraltar International Drama Festival. Read these rules before you enter your group.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Entries close on {{EntryDeadline}}. No late entries are accepted. A deposit of {{EntryDeposit}} is needed with the entry. The script and programme details are due by {{ScriptDeadline}}.","Notes":["The Festival is for amateur drama groups. Plays must be in English.","The Festival runs on {{FestivalDates}} at {{Venue}}.","Entry to the Festival is free. A deposit is paid with the entry and is refunded if the group gives a public performance.","Questions go to the Festival Director and Administrator Team: {{FestivalContact}}."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Gibraltar International Drama Festival (the Festival) is held to promote the production and performance of amateur drama in Gibraltar.","The Festival is organised by Gibraltar Cultural Services (the Organiser).","The Festival dates can change depending on the number of entries.","Plays must be in the English language.","The Organiser can refuse any entry without giving a reason.","The Organiser can make any regulations, interpret them or qualify any Festival rule as needed and without prior notice.","The Organiser decides the order in which the plays are performed. The Organiser's decision on the order of rehearsals and performances, or on any other matter arising from the rules or connected to the Festival, is final.","The Organiser appoints a Festival Director and Administrator Team. This team is the official point of contact for any queries from groups about the Festival.","The Organiser appoints a Festival Stage Director. The Stage Director's decisions on all backstage matters are final and binding on all groups.","The Organiser appoints a Festival Technical Director. The Technical Director's decisions on all lights and sound matters are final and binding on all groups.","The Organiser appoints a Front of House Manager.","The roles of the Festival Director and Administrator Team, Stage Director, Technical Director and Front of House Manager are to assist, guide, train and support all the participants in the Festival.","Each group is given a number of free tickets to the Festival, including the Gala Night.","Groups cannot advertise their play commercially on their own. The Organiser has sole responsibility for marketing the Festival.","The Organiser arranges online coverage of the Festival on its social media platforms."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Adult amateur groups can enter. An adult group is a society that is mainly for people over the statutory school leaving age.","Youth groups can enter. A youth group is a society in which all acting parts are played by young participants aged 17 or under.","Young participants aged 16 or under must be accompanied by a responsible adult at all times.","Dramatic schools that train professional actors cannot enter the Festival.","Groups cannot use the services of any professional director or actor. A professional is a person who does this work full time as their only means of living.","A group cannot enter the same play again until five years have passed.","A group can enter more than one play.","The entry must be a one-act play with more than one actor, an extract from a longer play, or another form of theatrical performance approved by the Organiser.","Youth players must be clearly identified in the team details and their dates of birth must be given.","Failure to give all the relevant documents makes the application ineligible."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Complete the Entry Form and submit it by {{EntryDeadline}}. No late entries are accepted.","The Entry Form must be signed by the Group Director to show that the group accepts the rules and conditions of entry.","The Entry Form must include copies of all the documents it asks for.","Give the composition of the team and each person's area of responsibility (for example Director, Producer, Technicians, Stage Managers) in the format the Organiser asks for.","Send a copy of the script by {{ScriptDeadline}}. Clearly mark any changes to the original script. Send the programme details by the same date.","The Organiser reads the scripts. If the Organiser thinks a play may cause offence, it can bar the play from performing or accept it on a restricted non-competing basis.","Complete the Props and Equipment List in the Programme Details Form and send it to the Organiser by the date given.","Pay the entry deposit of {{EntryDeposit}} when you submit the entry.","Copyright plays: the group must get the author's permission at its own expense. A copy of the licence must be given to the Organiser by the closing date.","Music: the group must get the necessary licences from the Performing Rights Society at its own expense. A copy of the licence must be given to the Organiser by the closing date.","No amendments, additions or deletions can be made to any play unless the author gives written consent to the Organiser. A group that does not follow this is disqualified.","A group that withdraws without a good reason after its entry is accepted can lose its deposit. The Organiser can ban the group from future festivals or admit it only on special terms.","A group that withdraws within one month before the start of the Festival loses all money paid. It must also pay back any money the Organiser paid to it.","By entering, a group agrees to give a public performance and is expected to appear, even if a main part has to be read.","Entry form: {{EntryFormLink}}."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Deposit","Items":["Entry of plays in the Festival is free.","A deposit of {{EntryDeposit}} is needed when the entry is submitted.","The deposit is refunded if the group gives a public performance at the Festival.","The deposit is not refunded if the Organiser decides the group withdrew without a valid reason.","A group that withdraws within one month before the start of the Festival loses all money paid.","Audience tickets are sold separately. Prices printed for the 2026 edition: {{TicketPrices}}."]},{"Key":"payments","Title":"Grants and Payments to Groups","Items":["After the Festival, a group can apply for an additional grant for its expenses, per entry.","A claim cannot be more than {{ExpenseGrantLimit}} per entry.","A claim can only be made for expenses directly caused by taking part in the Festival.","Payments are made when the group shows clear and detailed receipts.","The receipts must be given to the Organiser within 10 working days of the end of the Festival.","If the winning play qualifies to compete at the National Drama Festival UK, the Festival offers a bursary of {{NationalFestivalBursary}}. The Festival is a member of the National Drama Festival Association."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Important Dates","Items":["Festival dates: {{FestivalDates}}.","Entries close on {{EntryDeadline}}.","The script and programme details are due by {{ScriptDeadline}}.","The receipts for an expense claim are due within 10 working days of the end of the Festival.","After the Festival, all sets, props and furniture must be removed within five days.","Sessions started at {{SessionStartTime}} in the 2026 edition."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue and Stage","Items":["All performances are held at {{Venue}}.","The Organiser provides the theatre, including its stage lighting and sound facilities, and the Front of House organisation.","The stage is 6 metres wide and 7 metres deep.","The Organiser gives each group rehearsal slots.","Groups must follow all the rules of Ince's Hall Theatre.","The Organiser gives each group a prop storage area backstage and a changing room.","Sets and props can be stored in the backstage basement, in the area the Organiser gives to each group. No set or furniture can be stored on stage during rehearsals.","Space for storing props and equipment is limited, so groups are advised not to use large sets or props. Groups are welcome to visit the theatre to check the size. Arrange visits with the Organiser."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Stage Rules","Items":["The group must find the props and equipment it needs. The Organiser must agree to the use of all equipment on Health and Safety and other grounds. If the Organiser limits a proposal, it tells the group, and the Organiser's decision is final.","The group's Technical Director or Stage Director is responsible for the switchboard and lighting equipment, under the direction of the group's Director or Stage Manager.","Each group must see that the lights are set correctly. Lights or stage lamp sockets connected to the dimmer packs cannot be moved in any way.","Any change to the lighting plot must be made within the time allowed for setting and striking.","Each group must appoint suitable people to supervise the setting and striking of the set, to make sure the curtains open and close at the right time, and to operate the sound and light equipment during the performance.","Nothing can be stuck or glued on the stage curtains or backdrop.","No paint, spray, glitter or foam of any type is allowed on stage.","The backdrop cannot be removed for any performance.","No recorded speech, film or TV material can be used without the written consent of the copyright holder.","Performances cannot be recorded, filmed or televised.","Groups must leave the dressing rooms, toilets and backstage area clean and tidy at all times.","Once the Festival ends, all sets, props and furniture must be removed within five days.","Any item left behind after the Festival is thrown away by the Organiser at the group's expense.","Any damage or loss to the theatre or equipment is the sole responsibility of the user during the allocated rehearsal and performing slots. The Organiser can charge for the repair or replacement of equipment found damaged after a group's use.","The Organiser is not liable for loss of or damage to sets, props, costumes, furniture, property or other theatrical equipment during the Festival. Groups are advised to get insurance.","Group Directors must make sure their cast and staff follow the rules and conditions of entry.","The Organiser can disqualify an individual or a group for not following the Festival rules.","Groups and other related people must not communicate with the Adjudicator before or during the Festival. Failure to do so can lead to disqualification."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Adjudication","Items":["The Organiser contracts an Adjudicator especially for the event.","The Adjudicator gives a public adjudication of each entry that performs in the Festival. The aim is constructive criticism that helps both the group and the audience.","The Adjudicator does not tell the marks or the order of merit in public.","Each group gets a written report with a summary of the Adjudicator's feedback on its performance.","The Adjudicator's decision is final.","The Adjudicator chooses a number of plays for the Gala Night. The Gala Night includes the top two or three plays, depending on their timings, and the winning play of the Festival (Best Play).","The Adjudicator can decide not to give a prize if the standard is not good enough, there are too few entries, or groups have broken the rules."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Marking for Best Play","Items":["The Best Play Award is marked out of 100 points.","Points are given for Acting, Production and Endeavour, Originality, Stage Presentation and Theatrical Attainment.","The source does not print how many points each of these five criteria carries."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Awards and Prizes","Items":["The awards are: Adjudicator's Award, Best Set Presentation, Best Technical Presentation, Best Supporting Actor, Best Supporting Actress, Best Supporting Youth Actor, Best Supporting Youth Actress, Best Actress, Best Youth Actress, Best Actor, Best Youth Actor, Best Director, Best Original Script and Best Play.","Each winner receives a trophy.","The group that wins the Best Play Award also receives a cash prize of {{BestPlayPrize}}.","Trophies are given at the Gala Night prize giving ceremony."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Entries per Group","Items":["Each group must name its team and the area each person is responsible for."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules (PDF)","Url":"https://www.culture.gi/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Gibraltar-International-Drama-Festival-2026-Rules.pdf"},{"Title":"Festival entry form (online)","Url":"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfN1nhteTB68QjbI9j6a6QmSrFumzejkZJzV4ZWE-oI3q5A_A/viewform"},{"Title":"Gibraltar Cultural Services forms page","Url":"https://www.culture.gi/forms"},{"Title":"Press release: 69th Festival programme and tickets","Url":"https://www.gibraltar.gov.gi/press-releases/69th-gibraltar-international-drama-festival-2026-782026-11687"}]}`),r=[],n=[{AgeGroup:"Youth",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, ENTRY clause 1b",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["A youth group is a society in which all acting parts are played by young participants aged 17 or under.","Young participants aged 16 or under must be accompanied by a responsible adult at all times.","Youth players must be clearly identified in the team details and their dates of birth must be given.","Youth awards: Best Supporting Youth Actor, Best Supporting Youth Actress, Best Youth Actress and Best Youth Actor."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- A youth group is a society in which all acting parts are played by young participants aged 17 or under.
- Young participants aged 16 or under must be accompanied by a responsible adult at all times.
- Youth players must be clearly identified in the team details and their dates of birth must be given.
- Youth awards: Best Supporting Youth Actor, Best Supporting Youth Actress, Best Youth Actress and Best Youth Actor.`},{AgeGroup:"Adult",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, ENTRY clause 1a",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["An adult group is a society that is mainly for people over the statutory school leaving age.","The awards for Best Supporting Actor, Best Supporting Actress, Best Actress and Best Actor are for the adult performers."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- An adult group is a society that is mainly for people over the statutory school leaving age.
- The awards for Best Supporting Actor, Best Supporting Actress, Best Actress and Best Actor are for the adult performers.`}],i=[{Title:"One-Act Play",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, PERFORMANCE and ADJUDICATION sections",Sections:{About:["The entry must be one of three things: a one-act play with more than one actor, an extract from a longer play, or another form of theatrical performance approved by the Organiser.","An extract must make sense to an audience that has not seen the full play."],TimeAndFormat:["Each performance must be at least 20 minutes and no more than 55 minutes. A ten-minute allowance can be given at the Adjudicator's discretion.","Curtain calls are not allowed.","Points are deducted for a performance that is longer than 1 hour and 5 minutes.","Each group has a maximum of 10 minutes to set the stage and 5 minutes to strike it. These times are extra to the playing time.","The Organiser appoints an official timekeeper. Penalties can be given for not keeping to the times.","Pre-recorded material must not be more than 10% of the whole production time."],Rules:["Monologues and one-actor plays that use pre-recorded acting scenes from different actors are not accepted.","Groups must perform in the order stated in the programme.","The Organiser sets the order of performances. It considers the need for a balanced evening of entertainment and the total length of the performances each evening."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["The Best Play Award is marked out of 100 points. Points are given for Acting, Production and Endeavour, Originality, Stage Presentation and Theatrical Attainment."],Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The entry must be one of three things: a one-act play with more than one actor, an extract from a longer play, or another form of theatrical performance approved by the Organiser.
- An extract must make sense to an audience that has not seen the full play.

## Time and format
- Each performance must be at least 20 minutes and no more than 55 minutes. A ten-minute allowance can be given at the Adjudicator's discretion.
- Curtain calls are not allowed.
- Points are deducted for a performance that is longer than 1 hour and 5 minutes.
- Each group has a maximum of 10 minutes to set the stage and 5 minutes to strike it. These times are extra to the playing time.
- The Organiser appoints an official timekeeper. Penalties can be given for not keeping to the times.
- Pre-recorded material must not be more than 10% of the whole production time.

## Rules
- Monologues and one-actor plays that use pre-recorded acting scenes from different actors are not accepted.
- Groups must perform in the order stated in the programme.
- The Organiser sets the order of performances. It considers the need for a balanced evening of entertainment and the total length of the performances each evening.

## Judging
- The Best Play Award is marked out of 100 points. Points are given for Acting, Production and Endeavour, Originality, Stage Presentation and Theatrical Attainment.`}],s=[],o=[{Key:"FestivalDates",Kind:"text",Label:"Festival dates",Value:"Monday 23 to Friday 27 March 2026 (the Gala Night is on the last day)",Source:"Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (Ref. 78/2026, 6 Feb 2026); the Rules PDF printed Monday 23 to Saturday 28 March 2026, dates subject to change depending on entries"},{Key:"EntryDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to submit the entry",Value:"2025-12-15",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, ENTRY clause 4 and closing line"},{Key:"ScriptDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to send the script and programme details",Value:"2026-02-20",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, ENTRY clause 5"},{Key:"EntryDeposit",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry deposit",Value:"GBP 100 per entry, refunded if the group gives a public performance",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, ENTRY clause 3"},{Key:"ExpenseGrantLimit",Kind:"fee",Label:"Largest expense claim per entry",Value:"GBP 200",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, FINANCES clause 1"},{Key:"BestPlayPrize",Kind:"fee",Label:"Cash prize for the Best Play",Value:"GBP 1,000",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, ADJUDICATION clause 9"},{Key:"NationalFestivalBursary",Kind:"fee",Label:"Bursary for the winning play at the National Drama Festival UK",Value:"up to GBP 4,000",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, ADJUDICATION clause 11"},{Key:"TicketPrices",Kind:"fee",Label:"Audience ticket prices (2026 edition)",Value:"GBP 12.00 per session, GBP 15.00 for the Gala Night, GBP 50.00 season ticket, GBP 25.00 student season ticket; sales opened from Monday 9 February 2026 at www.buytickets.gi",Source:"Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (Ref. 78/2026, 6 Feb 2026)"},{Key:"SessionStartTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Session start time",Value:"7pm",Source:"Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (Ref. 78/2026, 6 Feb 2026)"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Festival venue",Value:{Name:"Ince's Hall Theatre",Address:"",City:"Gibraltar",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules, PRESENTATION clause 1 and 17. The Rules print no street address."},{Key:"FestivalContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact for questions",Value:{Name:"Gibraltar Cultural Services, Events Department",Role:"Festival Director and Administrator Team",Phone:"20067236",WhatsApp:"",Email:"info@culture.gi"},Source:"Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (entry call) and Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (Ref. 78/2026, 6 Feb 2026)"},{Key:"EntryFormLink",Kind:"link",Label:"Online entry form",Value:"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfN1nhteTB68QjbI9j6a6QmSrFumzejkZJzV4ZWE-oI3q5A_A/viewform",Source:"Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (entry call)"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News and announcements",Value:[{Date:"2026-02-06",Title:"69th Festival programme",Text:"The 2026 Festival ran from Monday 23 to Friday 27 March at Ince's Hall Theatre. Each session started at 7pm. On Friday 27 March the Gala Night staged the top two plays and the overall winner, followed by the awards ceremony. Ticket sales opened from Monday 9 February 2026.",Url:"https://www.gibraltar.gov.gi/press-releases/69th-gibraltar-international-drama-festival-2026-782026-11687"},{Date:"",Title:"Entry call for 2026",Text:"Groups were asked to enter through the online form by Monday 15 December 2025. The press release says each participating group receives a small grant towards production costs, and that non-competitive entries are also accepted.",Url:"https://www.gibraltar.gov.gi/press-releases/69th-gibraltar-international-drama-festival-2026-11355"}],Source:"Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (Ref. 78/2026, 6 Feb 2026) and Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (entry call)"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, eligibility, entry, finances, performance, presentation, adjudication, awards and general conditions captured from the organiser's own 2026 Rules PDF (8 pages).",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules",Source:"Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 Rules",Url:"https://www.culture.gi/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Gibraltar-International-Drama-Festival-2026-Rules.pdf"},{Claim:"Newer festival dates (ended Friday 27 March), session time, ticket prices and organiser contact taken from the organiser's 2026 press releases.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own announcement",Source:"Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (Ref. 78/2026, 6 Feb 2026)",Url:"https://www.gibraltar.gov.gi/press-releases/69th-gibraltar-international-drama-festival-2026-782026-11687"},{Claim:"Entry form link, grant and non-competitive entry note taken from the entry call.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own announcement",Source:"Gibraltar Government press release 69th Gibraltar International Drama Festival 2026 (entry call)",Url:"https://www.gibraltar.gov.gi/press-releases/69th-gibraltar-international-drama-festival-2026-11355"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:r,AgeGroups:n,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:o,Evidence:l};export{n as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,a as Page,r as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,o as Variables,h as Year,d as default};
